o How do child routes and lazy loading improve the structure and performance of an Angular
application?
- Child routes let you organize your app into smaller sections, like having subpages under a
main page. Lazy loading makes the app faster by only loading the parts you need when you
need them. Together, they keep your app neat and quick by loading less stuff upfront.
o What is the purpose of route guards, and how do they enhance the security of an application?
- Route guards are like bouncers for your app, controlling who can access different pages.
They check if a user is allowed to go to a route (like a profile page) before letting them in.
This enhances security by blocking unauthorized access and making sure only the right
people can reach sensitive areas or perform certain actions.

